1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:02,429
Diya is preparing for NEET.

2
00:00:02,429 --> 00:00:05,730
Its subjects are Physics,
Chemistry and Biology.

3
00:00:06,130 --> 00:00:11,038
Her PUC science subjects are Physics,
Chemistry, Maths and Biology.

4
00:00:11,488 --> 00:00:14,678
She noticed something while
filling in her study timetable.

5
00:00:15,028 --> 00:00:18,066
Every NEET subject is also a PUC subject.

6
00:00:18,066 --> 00:00:21,957
But Maths is a PUC subject,
and not a NEET subject.

7
00:00:21,957 --> 00:00:23,760
It only works one way.

8
00:00:24,260 --> 00:00:27,416
That one way link between
two sets has a name.

9
00:00:27,416 --> 00:00:28,316
A subset.

10
00:00:28,888 --> 00:00:30,241
So what is a subset?

11
00:00:30,591 --> 00:00:35,249
A set A is a subset of a set B if
every element of A is also an element

12
00:00:35,249 --> 00:00:36,149
of B.

13
00:00:36,258 --> 00:00:39,398
We write A, then this
sideways U symbol, then B.

14
00:00:39,398 --> 00:00:41,472
It reads: A is a subset of B.

15
00:00:41,872 --> 00:00:43,247
Watch the check run.

16
00:00:43,247 --> 00:00:47,444
Take each element of the NEET set,
and look for it in the PUC set.

17
00:00:47,844 --> 00:00:48,744
Physics?

18
00:00:48,554 --> 00:00:49,454
Found.

19
00:00:49,165 --> 00:00:50,065
Chemistry?

20
00:00:49,975 --> 00:00:50,875
Found.

21
00:00:50,585 --> 00:00:51,485
Biology?

22
00:00:51,296 --> 00:00:52,196
Found.

23
00:00:51,906 --> 00:00:55,308
Every element passed, so
NEET is a subset of PUC.

24
00:00:55,708 --> 00:00:57,120
Now the other way.

25
00:00:57,120 --> 00:00:58,358
Physics, found.

26
00:00:58,358 --> 00:00:59,698
Chemistry, found.

27
00:00:59,698 --> 00:01:00,598
Maths?

28
00:01:00,318 --> 00:01:01,892
Not in the NEET set.

29
00:01:01,892 --> 00:01:03,506
One failure is enough.

30
00:01:03,506 --> 00:01:05,608
PUC is not a subset of NEET.

31
00:01:06,258 --> 00:01:08,862
Two facts follow straight
from the definition.

32
00:01:09,262 --> 00:01:10,162
First.

33
00:01:09,825 --> 00:01:11,921
Every set is a subset of itself.

34
00:01:11,921 --> 00:01:14,589
Each element of A is, of course, in A.

35
00:01:15,339 --> 00:01:16,239
Second.

36
00:01:15,970 --> 00:01:18,590
The empty set is a subset of every set.

37
00:01:18,590 --> 00:01:21,449
It has no element that
could fail the check.

38
00:01:22,199 --> 00:01:23,536
Now, equal sets.

39
00:01:23,536 --> 00:01:27,367
Two sets are equal if they
have exactly the same elements.

40
00:01:27,767 --> 00:01:29,310
Here is a neat test.

41
00:01:29,310 --> 00:01:34,066
A equals B exactly when A is a
subset of B, and B is a subset of A.

42
00:01:34,066 --> 00:01:35,588
Check both directions.

43
00:01:36,338 --> 00:01:39,134
The letters of ALLOY and
the letters of LOYAL.

44
00:01:39,134 --> 00:01:40,908
Both give A, L, O, Y.

45
00:01:40,908 --> 00:01:44,310
Order and repeats do not
matter, so the sets are equal.

46
00:01:44,910 --> 00:01:50,345
If A is a subset of B, but A is not
equal to B, A is called a proper subset

47
00:01:50,345 --> 00:01:51,245
of B.

48
00:01:50,993 --> 00:01:53,313
NEET is a proper subset of PUC.

49
00:01:53,913 --> 00:01:56,673
Our number sets fit inside
each other like this.

50
00:01:57,073 --> 00:01:58,505
N is inside Z.

51
00:01:58,505 --> 00:01:59,936
Z is inside Q.

52
00:01:59,936 --> 00:02:01,367
Q is inside R.

53
00:02:01,367 --> 00:02:07,188
And T, the irrational numbers like
root two and pi, also sits inside R.

54
00:02:07,788 --> 00:02:10,057
But N is not a subset of T.

55
00:02:10,057 --> 00:02:12,402
No natural number is irrational.

56
00:02:13,002 --> 00:02:14,135
Side by side.

57
00:02:14,135 --> 00:02:16,507
Two symbols that students mix up.

58
00:02:16,907 --> 00:02:19,229
Belongs to joins an element to a set.

59
00:02:19,229 --> 00:02:21,822
One belongs to the set one, two, three.

60
00:02:22,422 --> 00:02:24,403
Subset joins a set to a set.

61
00:02:24,403 --> 00:02:28,050
The set containing one is a
subset of one, two, three.

62
00:02:28,050 --> 00:02:29,965
Curly brackets on both sides.

63
00:02:30,565 --> 00:02:31,504
Now you try.

64
00:02:31,504 --> 00:02:35,405
Is it correct to write: one is
a subset of one, two, three?

65
00:02:35,405 --> 00:02:36,571
Pause and decide.

66
00:02:39,771 --> 00:02:40,671
No!

67
00:02:40,205 --> 00:02:42,295
One is an element, not a set.

68
00:02:42,295 --> 00:02:44,236
Write one belongs to the set.

69
00:02:44,236 --> 00:02:47,485
Or put one in curly brackets,
and then use subset.

70
00:02:48,135 --> 00:02:49,232
Remember this.

71
00:02:49,232 --> 00:02:52,963
A is a subset of B when
every element of A is in B.

72
00:02:52,963 --> 00:02:55,279
Equal sets are subsets both ways.

73
00:02:55,979 --> 00:02:57,715
Now, one worked example.

74
00:02:58,065 --> 00:02:59,335
A is one, three.

75
00:02:59,335 --> 00:03:00,981
B is one, five, nine.

76
00:03:00,981 --> 00:03:03,559
C is one, three, five, seven, nine.

77
00:03:03,559 --> 00:03:06,467
Put subset, or not
subset, between each pair.

78
00:03:06,967 --> 00:03:07,867
One.

79
00:03:07,487 --> 00:03:09,067
The empty set and B.

80
00:03:09,067 --> 00:03:13,034
Phi is a subset of every
set, so phi is a subset of B.

81
00:03:13,784 --> 00:03:14,684
Two.

82
00:03:14,315 --> 00:03:15,215
A and B.

83
00:03:15,179 --> 00:03:18,092
Three is in A, but three is not in B.

84
00:03:18,092 --> 00:03:20,204
So A is not a subset of B.

85
00:03:20,954 --> 00:03:21,854
Three.

86
00:03:21,595 --> 00:03:22,495
A and C.

87
00:03:22,467 --> 00:03:24,641
One and three are both in C.

88
00:03:24,641 --> 00:03:26,500
So A is a subset of C.

89
00:03:27,250 --> 00:03:28,150
Four.

90
00:03:27,850 --> 00:03:28,750
B and C.

91
00:03:28,740 --> 00:03:31,344
One, five and nine are all in C.

92
00:03:31,344 --> 00:03:33,242
So B is a subset of C.

93
00:03:33,892 --> 00:03:35,357
Now, the exam trap.

94
00:03:35,707 --> 00:03:37,657
A is the set one, two, three.

95
00:03:37,657 --> 00:03:40,170
Many students write: one is a subset of A.

96
00:03:40,570 --> 00:03:42,216
But one is an element.

97
00:03:42,216 --> 00:03:45,128
Elements belong, and
only sets are subsets.

98
00:03:45,128 --> 00:03:49,716
Write one belongs to A, or the set
containing one is a subset of A.

99
00:03:50,366 --> 00:03:51,880
Where is this asked?

100
00:03:51,880 --> 00:03:56,656
In PUC board exams, as fill in subset
or not subset, and which of these

101
00:03:56,656 --> 00:03:57,855
sets are equal.

102
00:03:58,455 --> 00:03:59,657
Exam level now.

103
00:03:59,657 --> 00:04:02,540
How many of these six statements are true?

104
00:04:02,540 --> 00:04:03,792
Pause and solve.

105
00:04:09,192 --> 00:04:10,455
The answer is C.

106
00:04:10,455 --> 00:04:11,355
Four.

107
00:04:11,504 --> 00:04:15,378
A has three elements: one, the
set containing two, and three.

108
00:04:15,378 --> 00:04:19,133
Two on its own is not an element,
so statement one is false.

109
00:04:19,633 --> 00:04:23,405
The set containing two is an
element, so statement two is true.

110
00:04:23,405 --> 00:04:26,488
Statement three is false,
because two is not in A.

111
00:04:26,988 --> 00:04:30,185
One and three are in A,
so statement four is true.

112
00:04:30,185 --> 00:04:34,557
The set holding the set two is a
subset too, so statement five is true.

113
00:04:35,057 --> 00:04:37,378
And phi is a subset of every set.

114
00:04:37,378 --> 00:04:39,075
Four statements are true.

115
00:04:39,675 --> 00:04:41,134
Here is your recap.

116
00:04:41,134 --> 00:04:42,634
Screenshot this card.

117
00:04:45,834 --> 00:04:48,671
Can you answer these three
questions without help?

118
00:04:49,071 --> 00:04:49,971
One.

119
00:04:49,545 --> 00:04:53,256
Is the set of vowels a
subset of the set a, b, c, d?

120
00:04:54,156 --> 00:04:55,056
Two.

121
00:04:54,643 --> 00:04:58,579
Are the letters of LISTEN and
the letters of SILENT equal sets?

122
00:04:59,479 --> 00:05:00,379
Three.

123
00:05:00,085 --> 00:05:03,068
Why is the empty set
a subset of every set?

124
00:05:04,168 --> 00:05:06,850
Next time: three snacks for a tiffin box.

125
00:05:06,850 --> 00:05:10,826
How many different ways can you
pack it, including an empty box?

126
00:05:10,826 --> 00:05:12,363
We meet the power set.
